       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. The reason you gave, having things settled before evening rounds because the family is visiting, isn't a clinical reason for a dose five times the maximum. It also doesn't change the risk to the patient. A 50 mg dose could cause profound hypotension and shock that can last for days, because amlodipine has a very long half-life.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a standard dose now.** For example, 5 mg by mouth once daily, or 10 mg if you want the maximum. The patient would start treatment today.\n- **Help with the timeline.** If the aim is to reach blood pressure control quickly, I can enter a standard amlodipine dose along with a note asking for a faster reassessment. You could also add or adjust another agent, based on your judgment.\n- **Route it to pharmacy or a physician.** If you think there's an unusual indication, a pharmacist or attending can review it and place the order through the hospital's override process.\n\nTell me which dose you'd like and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
